# Maintenance schedule (BusyBox cron, UTC).
#
# Every job runs as the unprivileged `nextjs` user — cron itself needs root, the jobs
# do not, and they touch the same data volume the application writes.
#
# Staggered on purpose: the integrity sweep reads a great deal from the same disk the
# backup container is reading at 02:15, so it runs before rather than during.

# Health monitor: disk, backups, restore drills, scanner, database. Alerts on change,
# stays quiet inside the cooldown window.
*/15 * * * *   su-exec nextjs sh /usr/local/bin/run.sh monitor

# Expired incomplete uploads. Hourly, because abandoned chunks hold disk the quota
# system has already counted against somebody.
7 * * * *      su-exec nextjs sh /usr/local/bin/run.sh cleanup:uploads

# Storage integrity: does every version row still have its bytes, and do a sampled 2%
# still hash to what was recorded. Runs before the backup window.
30 1 * * *     su-exec nextjs sh /usr/local/bin/run.sh verify:storage

# Trash past its retention window. Permanent deletion of research data is deliberately
# a scheduled, auditable job rather than a TTL index.
0 3 * * *      su-exec nextjs sh /usr/local/bin/run.sh purge:trash

# ── Google Shared Drive storage ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# All three are no-ops when GOOGLE_DRIVE_STORAGE_ENABLED is false, so this file is the
# same on a deployment that has not switched Drive on. There is deliberately no job for
# archiving or deleting local copies: §18 of the storage brief requires explicit admin
# approval for those, and a scheduled job is the precise opposite of that.

# Uploads waiting to reach the Shared Drive. Large files are queued rather than
# transferred while the employee waits, and anything uploaded during a Drive outage is
# queued too. Frequent, because the queue holds local disk until it drains.
*/5 * * * *    su-exec nextjs sh /usr/local/bin/run.sh drive:drain

# Changes made directly in the Shared Drive — renames, trash, edits. Matches the default
# DRIVE_SYNC_INTERVAL_MINUTES; change both together or the System page will report a
# stall that is really a mismatched expectation.
*/15 * * * *   su-exec nextjs sh /usr/local/bin/run.sh drive:sync

# Approvals whose content lives in Drive: is each still the revision that was signed off?
# Hourly. Most changes are caught reactively by drive:sync above — this is the sweep that
# asks every question, and it is what catches whatever the change feed missed while its
# cursor was expired.
40 * * * *     su-exec nextjs sh /usr/local/bin/run.sh drive:check-approvals
